# KAPLAY Scenes Reference

## Core concepts

- Define scenes with `scene(name, callback)`.
- Switch scenes with `go(name, data?)`.
- Treat scenes as lifecycle boundaries: objects outside persistent mechanisms are destroyed on `go()`.

## Data passing

- Prefer object payloads for readability:
  - `go("world", { spawn, area })`
  - `scene("world", ({ spawn, area }) => { ... })`

## Persistence

- Use `stay()` on objects that should survive scene transitions (e.g. debug widgets, persistent overlays).
- Keep scene initialization inside scene callbacks; avoid one-time setup that prevents re-entry.

## Practical guidelines

- Every player-facing mode should be a scene (menu, world, cutscene, etc.).
- Scene callback should only orchestrate:
  - asset usage
  - entity spawn
  - event wiring
  - camera setup
- Defer reusable logic to helper functions and `entities/` modules.
